# `"x" * n` accumulated with `Result := Result + s`, so it re-copied everything
# built so far on every iteration: 80k characters took 19 SECONDS and 100k never
# finished. Content was always right, which is why only a scaling curve found it.
# bug-nilpy-str-repeat-is-quadratic
#
# The large sizes below are the actual regression guard -- under the old
# quadratic routine this file would not complete. Keep them large.

# content first: every shape must be byte-identical to CPython's
print("x" * 5, "ab" * 3, "abc" * 2)
print(3 * "ab")
print("[" + "ab" * 0 + "]", "[" + "ab" * -1 + "]", "[" + "" * 5 + "]")
print(len("x" * 1), len("abcd" * 250))

# ...then the sizes that were intolerable
print(len("x" * 80000))
print(len("ab" * 100000))
print(len("x" * 1000000))

# a repeated multi-character string must still be correct at size, not just long
big = "abc" * 100000
print(len(big), big[0], big[1], big[2], big[299999])
